# SPEED & EFFICIENCY DIRECTIVES (Lovable Mode)
1. NO OVER-PLANNING: For simple UI, text, color, style, or layout requests, DO NOT generate a multi-step mission plan or deep thought log. Act directly.
2. GREP FIRST: When searching for UI text, labels, classes, or copy, run a single targeted ripgrep/grep search for the exact user-visible text. Never read whole directory trees.
3. CONFINED SCOPE: Only inspect and modify the exact file containing the component. Do not touch routing, state, types, or related files unless explicitly broken.
4. TARGETED DIFFS: Apply surgical inline changes. Do not re-write or re-output entire files.
5. NO AUTO-TESTING: Do not run builds, linter suites, or spawn headless browser sessions for visual checks unless explicitly requested.
6. Run in Turbo mode. Do not spawn browser sessions or visual verification. Apply the styling updates directly, and exit.